# Inline assembly checked with Isla (verus/ISLA.md) up to the SVC
# exception it takes, so the kernel's side of the call stays unchecked:
# run.sh checks each against the contract verus/isla/seams.md quotes.
# `#2` is the aarch64 `mod imp` (`#1` the x86_64 one).
syscall0#2	inline asm	Islaris/Isla	trusted (partly checked, Isla: verus/isla/seams.md; not checked: the kernel's side of the call)
syscall1#2	inline asm	Islaris/Isla	trusted (partly checked, Isla: verus/isla/seams.md; not checked: the kernel's side of the call)
syscall2#2	inline asm	Islaris/Isla	trusted (partly checked, Isla: verus/isla/seams.md; not checked: the kernel's side of the call)
syscall3#2	inline asm	Islaris/Isla	trusted (partly checked, Isla: verus/isla/seams.md; not checked: the kernel's side of the call)
syscall4#2	inline asm	Islaris/Isla	trusted (partly checked, Isla: verus/isla/seams.md; not checked: the kernel's side of the call)
syscall5#2	inline asm	Islaris/Isla	trusted (partly checked, Isla: verus/isla/seams.md; not checked: the kernel's side of the call)
syscall6#2	inline asm	Islaris/Isla	trusted (partly checked, Isla: verus/isla/seams.md; not checked: the kernel's side of the call)
